{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeS6npAFDxLcB2oAJ179x","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`--dry-run` (short form `-n`) makes rsync **simulate the transfer without changing anything**. It walks through the file list, decides what it *would* copy, delete, or update, and reports that — but no files are written, deleted, or modified on either side.\n\nTypical use:\n\n```sh\nrsync -avn --delete src/ dest/\n```\n\nThis shows the plan (which files would be sent, which would be removed because of `--delete`) so you can sanity-check paths and flags before running it for real. It's especially valuable with `--delete`, where a trailing-slash mistake can wipe a directory.\n\nHelpful companions:\n\n- `-v` / `-i` (`--itemize-changes`) — otherwise a dry run prints very little; `-i` shows a per-file code explaining *why* each file would be transferred.\n- `--stats` — summary counts of files that would be transferred.\n\nOne caveat: because no data is actually sent, the byte counts and speed figures in the dry-run summary are estimates, not real transfer numbers."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11672,"cache_read_input_tokens":8005,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11672},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e6a61fa-2d0d-4636-a443-e24462779fe5","uuid":"1b4d944d-7f49-4958-a2ca-af6c5a9d44e7","timestamp":"2026-08-26T21:51:50.050Z","request_id":"req_011CeS6nmnNZmtf5WmwpcvEi"}
